  "protocolVersion": null,
  "instructions": "DeckCraft makes and edits presentations. To make a new presentation, call deck_create. When the user attaches a presentation, its absolute path is provided in context: open that exact path with DeckCraft, inspect and edit the requested slides, save under a new name, then call file_attach so the user can download it. Never write Python or other code to create, read or edit a presentation. To give the user any file a tool wrote, call file_attach with its path.\n\nEditing: open_presentation (check missingFonts, damagedMedia and lostSlides in the reply) → inspect_document for the slide list → inspect_slide {index} for shape ids, placeholders, text and boxes (`overflow: true` marks text that doesn't fit) → set_text {id, text} to replace a shape's text (one paragraph per line, leading tabs indent; set_text acts on the current slide, so go_to_slide first) → render_slide to look at the result → save_presentation → file_attach. Every other change is a command: list_commands {filter} finds ids and parameters, run_command runs one and batch several, e.g. slide.new {layout, title, body, at}, slide.delete {index}, slide.move {from, to}, slide.duplicate, slide.notes {index, text}, format.bold / format.size / format.color on selected shapes (edit.select {ids}), table.* and chart.data {id, categories, series}. Coordinates are points (the 16:9 slide is 960×540, y down). Formatting, layouts, notes, tables, charts and pictures that DeckCraft models are kept when saving; anything it does not model in an uploaded file may not survive, so mention import warnings to the user. Backend: headless (in-process engine; no window). Community: https://discord.gg/artcraft (Discord), https://getartcraft.com/apps/deckcraft (app page), https://github.com/storytold/deckcraft (source).",
  "durationMs": 2452,
  "stderr": "deckcraft-cli: files confined: read roots /pkg, write roots /pkg; saves create new files only\n"
}
